    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "A client's page now shows how many projects and contacts that client has, and `bin/e2e` passes. The test seeds a second client that also has a project and a contact, and Acme correctly shows 2 projects and 3 contacts.\n\n**Server**\n- I added `GET /api/clients/{id}/summary`, which returns `{ projectCount, contactCount }`. It returns 404 for an unknown client.\n- The counts come from two new count queries, one on the projects table and one on the contacts table, filtered by client id (`countByClientId`). They are wired in `ClientService.summary` and exposed by `ClientController`, with a new `ClientSummaryResponse` record.\n\n**Front end**\n- In `client-detail.ts`, two badges sit under the client's email: \"Projects: 2\" and \"Contacts: 3\". The test reads the numbers from `client-projects-count` and `client-contacts-count`.\n- The contacts section now sends an event when a contact is saved, and the client page re-fetches the counts. So the contact count stays correct after you add a contact on that page. Projects can't be added from this page, so their count can't go stale there.\n\n**Two departures from the brief:**\n- **No database migration.** The counts are worked out from the existing project and contact tables, so there was nothing to add to the schema.\n- **The server is Spring Boot, not OfficeFloor.** The code only uses `officefloor` as a package name, and CLAUDE.md describes a Spring app, so I followed Spring conventions.\n\nI didn't touch any existing `data-testid`, the `bin/` scripts or the spec.",
